      "name": "Fix",
      "summary": "Fix re-establishes the heap ordering after the element at index i has changed its value. Changing the value of the element at index i and then calling Fix is equivalent to, but less expensive than, calling [Remove](h, i) followed by a Push of the new value. The complexity is O(log n) where n = h.Len().",
